# Goal: identical changes on both branches still produce a merge commit.
I setup2.inc
> branch other
<<<
+ f.txt notwug.txt
> add f.txt
<<<
> commit "Change f on master"
<<<
> checkout other
<<<
+ f.txt notwug.txt
> add f.txt
<<<
> commit "Same change on other"
<<<
> checkout master
<<<
> merge other
<<<
= f.txt notwug.txt
= g.txt notwug.txt
> log
===
${COMMIT_HEAD}
Merged other into master\.

